{
  "title": "Metaphyseal Chondrodysplasia",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pediatrics/4099/metaphyseal-chondrodysplasia",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 16 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Metaphyseal Chondrodysplasia is a heterogeneous group of congenital disorders caused by variety of mutations leading to metaphyseal changes of the tubular bones with normal epiphyses. Patients present with short-limb dwarfism characterized by genu varum, coxa vara, and spinal abnormalities.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made based on family history associated with typical radiographic and clinical features. No commercially available diagnostic test exists due to the variety of genetic mutations.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment involves a multidisciplinary approach to improve and maintain function. Surgical spinal fusion is indicated in patients with atlantoaxial instability.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "skeletal dysplasias occur at a rate of 2 to 3 newborns per 10,000 births",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "metaphyseal dysplasia involving the **proliferative** and **hypertrophic** zone of the physis (epiphysis is normal)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Genetics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "three main subtypes",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Jansen (rare, most severe form)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**autosomal dominant**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "genetic defect in **parathryoid hormone-related peptide (PTHrP)**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "Schmid (more common, less severe form)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**autosomal dominant**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**genetic defect in type X collagen**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "McKusick",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**autosomal recessive**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**most commonly occurs in Amish and Finnish populations**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "cartilage-hair dysplasia (hypoplasia of cartilage and small diameter of hair)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**birth defects**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "can be mimicked by teratogenic",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**rickets**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Schmid type often confused for rickets",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
